!!!
%html
  %head
    %meta{:content => "text/html; charset=utf-8", "http-equiv" => "Content-Type"}/
    %meta{name: "viewport", content: "width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"}/
    %meta{name: "color-scheme", content: "only light"}/
    %meta{name: "supported-color-schemes", content: "light"}/
    :css
      html {
        color-scheme: only light;
        forced-color-adjust: none;
      }

      :root {
        color-scheme: only light;
        supported-color-schemes: light;
        forced-color-adjust: none;
      }

      body {
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
        background-color: #17231d;
        color: #21302a;
        color-scheme: only light;
        forced-color-adjust: none;
        font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
      }

      table {
        border-collapse: collapse;
      }

      .email-body p {
        margin: 0 0 18px;
        font-size: 17px;
        line-height: 1.55;
      }

      .email-body a {
        color: #1f6f55;
        font-weight: 700;
      }

      .email-body strong {
        color: #17231d;
      }

      .email-background,
      .email-card,
      .email-header {
        color-scheme: only light;
        forced-color-adjust: none;
      }

      @media only screen and (max-width: 640px) {
        .email-shell {
          width: 100% !important;
        }

        .email-card {
          padding: 28px 24px !important;
        }

        .email-header {
          padding-left: 24px !important;
          padding-right: 24px !important;
        }

        .email-logo-main {
          font-size: 34px !important;
        }

        .email-logo-sub {
          font-size: 20px !important;
        }
      }
  %body{style: "margin: 0; padding: 0; background-color: #17231d; color-scheme: only light; forced-color-adjust: none; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;"}
    %table{role: "presentation", width: "100%", cellpadding: "0", cellspacing: "0", style: "min-width: 100%; background-color: #17231d; color-scheme: only light; forced-color-adjust: none;"}
      %tr
        %td.email-background{align: "center", style: "background-color: #17231d; color-scheme: only light; forced-color-adjust: none; padding: 28px 12px;"}
          %table.email-shell{role: "presentation", width: "620", cellpadding: "0", cellspacing: "0", style: "width: 620px; max-width: 100%; background-color: #fffaf0;"}
            %tr
              %td.email-header{style: "background-color: #17231d; padding: 30px 34px 24px; color: #f8f4ea; text-align: left;"}
                %p{style: "margin: 0; color: #ffffff; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; line-height: 1;"}
                  %span.email-logo-main{style: "display: block; font-size: 42px; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: 0;"}
                    Cragmont
                  %span.email-logo-sub{style: "display: block; color: #ffffff; font-size: 22px; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: 0; text-transform: uppercase;"}
                    Climbing Club
            %tr
              %td.email-card.email-body{style: "background-color: #fffaf0; color: #21302a; padding: 36px 40px 32px;"}
                = yield
                %p.email-liability-note{style: "margin: 28px 0 0; padding-top: 18px; border-top: 1px solid #d8cfbd; color: #6f786f; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.45;"}
                  Cragmont is not a teaching organization. It's a social base camp. We create shared spaces to connect with other climbers. We hope you'll exchange knowledge and learn from one another. However, Cragmont does not test or vet members. It's up to you to decide what knowledge is correct and what might lead to danger. If you are new to climbing, the best way to help with these decisions is to take classes from professional guides.
